{"name":"Victorian Tapestry","hex":"#6c7773","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tapestry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy woven cloth, often with decorative pictorial designs, normally hung on walls.","Anything with variegated or complex details."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with tapestry, or as if with a tapestry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tapestry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tapestry","blocks":[{"text":"Tapestry is a form of textile art which was traditionally woven by hand on a loom. Normally it is used to create images rather than patterns. Tapestry is relatively fragile, and difficult to make, so most historical pieces are intended to hang vertically on a wall, or sometimes to lie horizontally over a piece of furniture such as a table or bed. Some periods made smaller pieces, often long and narrow and used as borders for other textiles. Most weavers use a natural warp thread, such as wool, linen, or cotton. The weft threads are usually wool or cotton but may include silk, gold, silver, or other alternatives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Rea-Menzies_in_studio.jpg/330px-Rea-Menzies_in_studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tapestry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg/500px-The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg/1280px-The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg/500px-The_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the tapestries in the series The Hunt of the Unicorn: The Unicorn is Found, circa 1495–1505, The Cloisters, Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Hunt_of_the_Unicorn_Tapestry_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg/500px-Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg/1280px-Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg/500px-Tapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tapestry Room from Croome Court, moved to the Metropolitan Museum of Art, hung with made to measure 18th-century Gobelins tapestries, also covering the chairs. 1763–71","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATapestry_Room_from_Croome_Court_MET_DP341243.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg/500px-The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg/1280px-The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg/500px-The_Triumph_of_Fame_MET_DT4292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Triumph of Fame, probably Brussels, 1500s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/